<task id="060" project="messaging-communication-app-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Polling conversation/timeline component in `@spaarke/ui-components` (Fluent v9): interleaved email+chat, reply nesting, compose box, unread indicator, ~5s poll</title>
    <phase>W6 — UI (polling timeline + PCF accessories)</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>14</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>050</dependencies>
    <blocks>061, 063</blocks>
    <tags>frontend, fluent-ui, react, communication</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>New load-bearing shared-library React component (`.tsx`/`.ts` in `@spaarke/ui-components`) that becomes the R1 message surface; architecture-level decisions (poll loop + reducer state, interleaving/ordering model, reply nesting, unread tracking, EmailComposer sub-component reuse); blocks the PCF packaging (061) and quoting (063). ADR-021 (Fluent v9), ADR-012 (shared lib), ADR-028 (auth decoupling) bind; NFR-04 (no client-side ACS SDK) is a hard acceptance gate. FULL is non-negotiable.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W6</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>All-client TypeScript in `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/**`; disjoint by file + language from the concurrent BFF (C#) tracks. Within W6 this is the serial root — 061 packages it and 063 extends its composer — but it runs safely alongside other waves.</parallel-reason>
    <fr-refs>FR-10</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Build the **polling conversation/timeline component** in `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CommunicationTimeline/` (Fluent UI v9). This is the R1 message surface — the "Activities / portal-comments" async experience the design describes (§6.2). It renders a single thread and lets a user read + send messages; it stays current by **polling the BFF**, never by talking to ACS.

    The component MUST (FR-10):
    - **Render a thread** — email AND chat messages interleaved into one ordered list (chronological by sent/received time), each row **channel-badged** (Email vs Message), with **reply nesting** derived from `sprk_inreplyto`. Rows show sender, timestamp, `sprk_body` (respecting `sprk_bodyformat`), and attachment file cards.
    - **Compose/send box** — a compose area at the foot of the thread to author + send a new message via the BFF (the send endpoint from task 051, surfaced through the injected `authenticatedFetch`). Reuse `<EmailComposer/>` sub-components (`BodyEditor`, `AttachmentList`, `RecipientField` where relevant) rather than re-implementing — extend, do not fork (§11).
    - **Unread indicator** — surface the unread count from the BFF unread-count endpoint (task 050) and a visual "new messages" affordance; clear/advance last-seen as the user views.
    - **~5s poll** — poll the BFF thread-read + unread-count endpoints on a configurable ~5s interval (default 5000ms, prop-overridable per NFR-07); reflect newly-captured inbound/outbound messages within one poll cycle. Pause polling when the document/tab is hidden; resume on focus. Debounce/guard against overlapping in-flight polls.

    **Reads persisted `sprk_communication` records ONLY.** There is NO client-side ACS SDK in R1 (NFR-04) — the component never imports `@azure/communication-chat`, `@azure/communication-common`, `@azure/communication-identity`, or `@azure/communication-react`. Viewing history and syncing are pure Dataverse/BFF reads. The live-channel/WebSocket upgrade is the NEXT project and layers onto this same component — do not build it here.

    All network I/O flows through an injected `authenticatedFetch` prop + a small typed `communicationTimelineApi` service (thread-read, unread-count, send) — the component MUST NOT import `@spaarke/auth` directly (ADR-028 / shared-lib decoupling). Fluent UI v9 only (ADR-021): `@fluentui/react-components` + `makeStyles` + `tokens`; dark mode passes through the host `FluentProvider`; no hardcoded colors.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior React 18 + TypeScript developer fluent in Fluent UI v9 (`makeStyles`/`tokens`/`FluentProvider`) and polling/data-sync UI patterns (interval loop, visibility-gating, in-flight guard). Familiar with the shipped `<EmailComposer/>` engine + sub-components in `@spaarke/ui-components` and the `authenticatedFetch`-injection idiom (ADR-028 decoupling).
  </role>

  <goal>
    A `CommunicationTimeline` component exists in `@spaarke/ui-components`, exported via the lib barrel, that renders a thread's `sprk_communication` rows (email + chat interleaved, channel-badged, ordered, reply-nested from `sprk_inreplyto`), offers a compose/send box reusing `<EmailComposer/>` sub-components, shows an unread indicator, and polls the BFF every ~5s (configurable) reflecting new messages within one cycle. It reads persisted records only and contains NO ACS SDK import. No `@spaarke/auth` import (grep-verified). `npm run build` + `npm run lint` clean; dark-mode + semantic-token compliant (ADR-021).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      The design (§6.2, §8.6) locks R1's message UX to a **polling** conversation/timeline component — the Activities/portal-comments model — NOT a live open channel. Send → BFF → ACS; receive → Event Grid → BFF persists → the component **polls the BFF** and updates. Because R1 builds no live-channel client, there is no client-side ACS SDK anywhere in R1 (design §8.5/NFR-04); the composites-vs-headless and React-version questions belong to the next project.

      §11 Component Justification (concrete cost-of-doing-nothing): there is **NO** `*Timeline*`/`*Thread*`/`*Conversation*` component in `@spaarke/ui-components` today (design §2 inventory — `<EmailComposer/>` is compose/send-only; viewing is the OOB form one record at a time + a flat subgrid). The failure mode without this component is a named contract failure: FR-10 cannot be satisfied and there is no surface that renders a grouped email+chat thread or drives the unread poll (051/050 have no consumer). This does not overlap `<EmailComposer/>` — it VIEWS a thread and REUSES the composer's sub-components for the send box; it does not re-implement compose/send mechanics. Extension over new: reuse `BodyEditor`/`AttachmentList`/`RecipientField` from `EmailComposer/subcomponents/` rather than cloning them.

      ADR-026 Path-A exception (spec §ADR Tensions): R1's UI surface is the OOB main form + PCFs, not a Code Page — mirroring email-r4's shipped W4 pivot. This component is the render engine that task 061 packages as a form-bound PCF; being form-bound keeps it within ADR-006 (PCF for form binding). Cite the Path-A exception in the PR touching this UI surface.

      Reads are BFF-mediated (`docs/standards/DATA-ACCESS-DECISION-CRITERIA.md`): the timeline reads the BFF thread-read + unread-count endpoints (task 050), which are access-filtered per FR-08 — the component renders whatever the BFF returns and never re-derives privacy client-side.
    </background>
