  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-10">Render a thread (email + chat interleaved, channel-badged, ordered, reply nesting from `sprk_inreplyto`), a compose/send box, and an unread indicator; poll the BFF every ~5s; reflect a newly-captured inbound message within one poll cycle.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-04">R1 client code MUST NOT import ANY ACS SDK (`@azure/communication-*`). The component reads persisted `sprk_communication` records via the BFF only. Grep-verified NO ACS import.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent UI v9 ONLY (`@fluentui/react-components`); `makeStyles` + `tokens`; dark mode via host `FluentProvider`; no hardcoded colors; no v8/v0.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Component + sub-components MUST NOT import `@spaarke/auth`. Host injects `authenticatedFetch` via props; the timeline API service forwards it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Shared-library rules — the component lives in `@spaarke/ui-components`; no fork; export via the lib barrel; no cross-package source-path imports.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-026">Path-A exception: this component is packaged as a form-bound PCF (task 061), NOT a Code Page. Cite the exception in the PR. (Being form-bound keeps it within ADR-006.)</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-07">Poll interval is a configurable prop (default ~5000ms); pause when tab hidden; guard overlapping polls to bound BFF load.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">§11 — REUSE `<EmailComposer/>` sub-components for the compose box; do not clone `BodyEditor`/`AttachmentList`/`RecipientField`. State the FR-10 failure mode + the "no timeline component exists today" evidence in the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">No BFF publish-size / CVE obligations — this is client-only TypeScript (root §10 does not apply). Build via `npm run build` (dev) — NOT dotnet.</constraint>
  </constraints>

