  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read design §6.2 (polling timeline), §8.6 (OOB form + PCF host), §6.3 (quoting seam that 063 will extend), spec FR-10/FR-11/NFR-04/NFR-07, and the `<EmailComposer/>` sub-components (`BodyEditor`, `AttachmentList`, `RecipientField`) + `communicationApi.ts` error contract. Read the task-050 thread-read + unread-count endpoint shapes to lock the read model.</step>
    <step order="2">Read ADR-021 + `fluent-v9-component/SKILL.md` for Fluent v9 conventions; read `DATA-ACCESS-DECISION-CRITERIA.md` to confirm BFF-mediated reads.</step>
    <step order="3">Author `CommunicationTimeline.types.ts`: `TimelineMessage { id; channelType; sender; sentOn; body; bodyFormat; inReplyTo?; attachments[] }`, `TimelineThread`, `UnreadState`, `CommunicationTimelineProps { threadId; authenticatedFetch; bffBaseUrl; pollIntervalMs? (default 5000); onSendComplete? }`, and the reducer state/action union (`SET_THREAD`, `MERGE_POLL`, `SET_UNREAD`, `ADVANCE_LAST_SEEN`, `BEGIN_SEND`, `END_SEND`).</step>
    <step order="4">Author `communicationTimelineApi.ts`: `readThread(threadId, {authenticatedFetch, bffBaseUrl})`, `getUnreadCount(threadId, ...)`, `sendMessage(request, ...)` — thin typed wrappers over the injected `authenticatedFetch`; mirror `sendCommunication()`'s typed-error contract. NO ACS imports.</step>
    <step order="5">Author `hooks/useThreadPoll.ts`: a ~5s interval loop (prop-configurable) that calls `readThread` + `getUnreadCount`, pauses on `document.hidden` (Page Visibility), guards overlapping in-flight requests, and dispatches `MERGE_POLL`/`SET_UNREAD`. Clean up the interval on unmount.</step>
    <step order="6">Author the interleave/nesting model: a pure `buildTimeline(messages)` helper that orders all messages chronologically and computes reply nesting from `sprk_inreplyto` (parent → child indentation), channel-agnostic. Unit-testable in task 080's client scope or a colocated test.</step>
    <step order="7">Author the sub-components: `MessageRow.tsx` (sender/time/body-by-format/attachment cards + nesting indent), `ChannelBadge.tsx` (Email vs Message, semantic tokens), `UnreadIndicator.tsx` (count + "new messages" affordance), `TimelineComposeBox.tsx` (REUSES `BodyEditor` + `AttachmentList` + `RecipientField`; calls `sendMessage`).</step>
    <step order="8">Author `CommunicationTimeline.tsx`: `useReducer` state, `useThreadPoll`, render the ordered/nested list + unread indicator + compose box; `role="region"`/`aria-label` landmarks + a live region announcing new inbound messages. On send success, optimistically advance and let the next poll reconcile (echo-dedup is server-side). Three `makeStyles`-driven layout with semantic tokens.</step>
    <step order="9">Author `CommunicationTimeline/index.ts` barrel; add `export * from './components/CommunicationTimeline';` to shared-lib `src/index.ts`.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `npm run build` + `npm run lint` in `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/` (use `npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund` if a fresh install is needed; NOT `npm ci`). Both MUST be clean. Grep-verify NO `@azure/communication` import and NO `@spaarke/auth` import under `CommunicationTimeline/**` + `communicationTimelineApi.ts`.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` on the new files (focus: no ACS import, no `@spaarke/auth` import, poll-loop cleanup + in-flight guard, Fluent v9 semantic tokens, EmailComposer reuse not clone); `adr-check` against ADR-021/ADR-028/ADR-012/ADR-026 + `spec.md` (FR-10, NFR-04, NFR-07). Address Critical + High findings.</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (060 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (poll cadence default, interleave/nesting algorithm, which EmailComposer sub-components were reused, unread last-seen mechanism).</step>
  </steps>

