  <ui-tests>
    <ui-test>Renders a thread of mixed email + chat messages interleaved in chronological order, each channel-badged, with reply-nested rows from `sprk_inreplyto` — no console errors.</ui-test>
    <ui-test>Dark mode: the timeline, channel badges, and unread indicator render correctly under a dark `FluentProvider` (semantic tokens; no hardcoded colors).</ui-test>
    <ui-test>Polling: a message added to the (mocked) BFF thread-read response appears in the rendered list within one poll cycle (~5s) without a manual refresh.</ui-test>
    <ui-test>Unread indicator reflects the mocked unread-count and clears/advances as the thread is viewed.</ui-test>
    <ui-test>Compose box reuses `<EmailComposer/>` sub-components (BodyEditor/AttachmentList) and sends via the injected `authenticatedFetch` (mocked); attachment caps follow `CHAT-ATTACHMENT-POLICY.md`.</ui-test>
    <ui-test>Poll loop pauses when `document.hidden` and resumes on focus; overlapping in-flight polls are guarded; interval is cleaned up on unmount (no leak warning).</ui-test>
  </ui-tests>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`CommunicationTimeline` renders email + chat messages interleaved in chronological order, each channel-badged, with reply nesting derived from `sprk_inreplyto`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A compose/send box is present and sends via the BFF through the injected `authenticatedFetch`, reusing `<EmailComposer/>` sub-components (grep confirms import-from, not clone).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An unread indicator reflects the BFF unread-count and advances last-seen as the thread is viewed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The component polls the BFF thread-read + unread-count endpoints on a configurable ~5s interval (default 5000ms); a newly-captured inbound message appears within one poll cycle; polling pauses when the tab is hidden and guards overlapping requests.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The component reads persisted records only and contains NO ACS SDK import — grep confirms no `@azure/communication-*` anywhere under `CommunicationTimeline/**` or `communicationTimelineApi.ts` (NFR-04).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No `@spaarke/auth` import anywhere under `CommunicationTimeline/**` (ADR-028, grep-verified).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Only `@fluentui/react-components` + `makeStyles` + `tokens` used for styling; no hardcoded colors; dark mode passes through the host `FluentProvider` (ADR-021).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm run build` + `npm run lint` clean in `@spaarke/ui-components`; the shared-lib barrel exports `CommunicationTimeline`.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Task 061 packages this component as a form-bound PCF and deploys it to the OOB form; task 063 adds the bidirectional "quote into…" action to the compose box. Both build on this — keep the compose box's prefill path (initial body/format) prop-driven so 063 can inject quoted content without re-opening the component.

    The live-channel upgrade (headless `@azure/communication-chat` → WebSocket append/typing/receipts) is the NEXT project and layers onto THIS component (design §6.2). Do NOT add any ACS client SDK or WebSocket path in R1 — NFR-04 is a hard acceptance gate verified by dependency scan (spec Success Criterion 11).

    Reads are BFF-mediated + access-filtered (task 050 enforces FR-08); the component renders what the BFF returns and never re-derives privacy client-side.
  </notes>

